[{"insertText":{"location":{"index":21275,"tabId":"t.0"},"text":"Figure 3. The three pre-registered comparisons for each encoder: paired difference in chunk MSE with a 95% bootstrap interval over the 30 tasks, the number of tasks favouring RAID v8, and the Holm-corrected verdict.\n6.2 The gate needs corruption training\nThe development tasks contained the ablation that motivated the design (Figure 4, Appendix B). Adding the confidence and disagreement inputs without corruption training made the head worse than RAID v7 for all three encoders (MAE 0.757 vs 0.637). With corruption training, the same head was best (0.494, against 0.592 for k-NN). Without examples of a wrong direct prediction, the gate learns to trust the trunk whenever it is confident; the corrupted rows teach it the opposite case. On the development task where RAID v7 had failed in our earlier study (wine bottle on top of the cabinet), the MAE error was 1.192 for RAID v7, 0.705 for RAID v8 and 0.643 for k-NN.\n"}},{"updateTextStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":21275,"endIndex":22196,"tabId":"t.0"},"textStyle":{},"fields":"bold,italic,underline,link,weightedFontFamily,foregroundColor,baselineOffset"}},{"updateParagraphStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":21275,"endIndex":22196,"tabId":"t.0"},"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT"},"fields":"namedStyleType"}},{"updateParagraphStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":21491,"endIndex":21530,"tabId":"t.0"},"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"HEADING_2"},"fields":"namedStyleType"}},{"insertText":{"location":{"index":22196,"tabId":"t.0"},"text":"\n"}},{"updateParagraphStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":22196,"endIndex":22197,"tabId":"t.0"},"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"CENTER"},"fields":"namedStyleType,alignment"}},{"insertInlineImage":{"location":{"index":22196,"tabId":"t.0"},"uri":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ConstantinVictorBeatErtel/RAID/84e380715ea4bbb698c07e7ada226ac0857a5a74/paper/figures/fig4_dev_ablation.png","objectSize":{"width":{"magnitude":468,"unit":"PT"},"height":{"magnitude":640,"unit":"PT"}}}},{"insertText":{"location":{"index":22198,"tabId":"t.0"},"text":"Figure 4. Development tasks, no target training: chunk MSE of k-NN, RAID v7, the v8 gate without corruption training and the v8 gate with corruption training (10 tasks × 3 seeds per encoder). These are design data, not held-out results.\n6.3 With a few updates, the advantage shrinks and compute decides\nTable 3. Final tasks: chunk MSE after n target updates (mean over 30 tasks × 3 seeds; encoder tuning: MAE, seed 42) and the time per update on an NVIDIA A100 80GB PCIe.\n"}},{"updateTextStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":22198,"endIndex":22670,"tabId":"t.0"},"textStyle":{},"fields":"bold,italic,underline,link,weightedFontFamily,foregroundColor,baselineOffset"}},{"updateParagraphStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":22198,"endIndex":22670,"tabId":"t.0"},"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT"},"fields":"namedStyleType"}},{"updateParagraphStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":22435,"endIndex":22501,"tabId":"t.0"},"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"HEADING_2"},"fields":"namedStyleType"}},{"insertTable":{"rows":10,"columns":7,"location":{"index":22669,"tabId":"t.0"}}},{"insertText":{"location":{"index":22820,"tabId":"t.0"},"text":"—"}},{"insertText":{"location":{"index":22818,"tabId":"t.0"},"text":"0.366"}},{"insertText":{"location":{"index":22816,"tabId":"t.0"},"text":"0.352"}},{"insertText":{"location":{"index":22814,"tabId":"t.0"},"text":"0.339"}},{"insertText":{"location":{"index":22812,"tabId":"t.0"},"text":"0.364"}},{"insertText":{"location":{"index":22810,"tabId":"t.0"},"text":"SigLIP"}},{"insertText":{"location":{"index":22808,"tabId":"t.0"},"text":"RAID v8 head (ours)"}},{"insertText":{"location":{"index":22805,"tabId":"t.0"},"text":"—"}},{"insertText":{"location":{"index":22803,"tabId":"t.0"},"text":"0.342"}},{"insertText":{"location":{"index":22801,"tabId":"t.0"},"text":"0.346"}},{"insertText":{"location":{"index":22799,"tabId":"t.0"},"